## Production Readiness Checklist (Static Audit)

### Architecture
| Gate | Checks |
|---|---|
| Single Responsibility | Each function/class has one reason to change |
| DRY | No duplicated logic — shared helpers extracted |
| SOLID | Open/closed, Liskov substitution, interface segregation, dependency inversion |
| Loose coupling | Components depend on abstractions, not concrete types |
| Layer separation | UI / business logic / data access cleanly separated |

### Security
| Gate | Checks |
|---|---|
| Input validation | All external input validated at the boundary |
| SQL safety | Parameterized queries only — zero string concatenation |
| Secrets | No hardcoded credentials, keys, or tokens — use env vars |
| Auth boundary | Every protected operation checks auth before executing |
| Output encoding | User-controlled data escaped before rendering |
| Path traversal | File paths sanitized — no `../` exploitation possible |
| DoS surface | Input length limits, timeouts, pagination on unbounded lists |

### Code Quality
| Gate | Checks |
|---|---|
| No magic values | All literals replaced with named constants |
| No silent failures | No `except: pass`, no `.catch(() => {})`, no swallowed errors |
| No global mutation | No global mutable state |
| Type safety | Full type annotations / strict mode enabled |
| Function size | No function > ~50 lines without explicit justification |
| Nesting depth | Max 3 levels — deeper code extracted to named functions |
| Clear naming | Self-documenting names — no `d`, `tmp`, `x`, `data2` |
| No dead code | No commented-out blocks, unreachable code, unused variables |

### Performance
| Gate | Checks |
|---|---|
| Algorithm complexity | Not worse than problem requires |
| No N+1 queries | No DB calls inside loops |
| Resource cleanup | Files, connections, streams always closed |
| No blocking in async | Sync I/O not called from async contexts |
| Caching | Repeated expensive calls cached where appropriate |

### Reliability
| Gate | Checks |
|---|---|
| Retry/backoff | Transient failures (network, rate limits) handled with retry |
| Timeouts | All external calls have explicit timeouts |
| Graceful degradation | Partial failure does not crash the whole system |
| Idempotency | Write operations safe to retry |
| Logging | Errors and key operations logged at appropriate levels |

### Testability
| Gate | Checks |
|---|---|
| Pure business logic | Core logic in pure functions — no hidden I/O |
| Injectable deps | External dependencies injected, not hardcoded |
| Test coverage | Happy path + edges + error paths all covered |
| Meaningful assertions | Tests assert behaviour, not implementation details |

