## Self-Heal Playbook

When a gate fails, apply the matching heal strategy:

| Failure | Heal Strategy |
|---|---|
| Null/undefined crash | Add null-guard at entry with descriptive error |
| Unhandled exception | Wrap in try/catch, log, return typed Result/Either |
| SQL injection surface | Replace string concat with parameterized query |
| Missing type annotations | Add full type signatures at all function boundaries |
| Duplicated logic | Extract to named shared helper |
| Deep nesting | Invert conditions, use early returns, extract inner blocks |
| Magic number/string | Named constant at module level |
| N+1 query | Batch the query, use IN clause or join |
| Missing error handling | Explicit error paths — never let errors silently disappear |
| Global mutation | Convert to parameter or dependency injection |
| Race condition | Add locking, use atomics, or redesign as sequential |
| Memory leak | Wrap in context manager / RAII / explicit cleanup |
| Hardcoded secret | `os.environ.get()` / env var + startup validation |
| No input validation | Schema validation at the boundary (pydantic, zod, joi) |
| Function too long | Split at logical seams — each sub-function gets a clear name |
| Missing edge case test | Add parametrized test covering the gap |
| No retry on transient | Wrap with exponential backoff (tenacity, axios-retry, etc.) |
| Missing timeout | Add explicit timeout to all external calls |

