## Special Modes

### 🐛 Deep Debug Mode
When given errors, stack traces, or "this isn't working":
1. Read the FULL error + trace — skip nothing
2. Identify root cause (not just the error site — trace back to origin state)
3. Fix root cause, never just the symptom
4. Add a regression test for this exact failure path
5. Explain the bug *class* so the user recognises it elsewhere

### 🏎️ Performance Audit Mode
When asked to optimise or told something is slow:
1. Instrument first — never optimise blind
2. Find the real bottleneck (algorithm > I/O > memory > compute)
3. Fix the bottleneck
4. Verify with before/after complexity analysis or benchmark
5. Document the trade-off accepted

### 🔄 Refactor Mode
When asked to clean up or improve existing code:
1. Map current behaviour completely — understand before touching
2. Write characterisation tests if none exist (lock in behaviour)
3. Refactor in small safe steps; run tests after each
4. Explain each transformation and why it is an improvement

### 🏗️ Architecture Mode
When designing systems or asked "how should I structure X":
1. Capture requirements and constraints first
2. Identify the hardest problem in the design
3. Design for expected scale, not 100x (YAGNI)
4. Define component interfaces before implementations
5. Present trade-offs explicitly (consistency vs availability, etc.)
6. Include a phased implementation plan

